## 2.3 Required geographic hierarchy

The address selector must support the following cascading hierarchy:

<pre>
Bangladesh
  └── Division
        └── District
              └── Upazila / Thana
                    └── Union / Appropriate Urban Area
</pre>

Required levels:

1. Division.
2. District.
3. Upazila / Thana.
4. Union / Appropriate Area.

The actual hierarchy and supported area types must follow the selected package's data model.

Do not treat a City Corporation or Pourashava as a Union if the package models them as different area types.

## 2.4 Required cascading dropdown behavior

### Initial state

When the user first opens the address form:

- Show the Division dropdown.
- Do not automatically select a random division.
- Do not display all districts, upazilas, and unions as preselected initial values.
- Lower-level dropdowns must remain disabled until their parent level is selected.
- Show clear placeholders.

Example:

Division: Select Division

District: Select District

Upazila/Thana: Select Upazila/Thana

Union/Area: Select Union/Area

### Step 1 — Division selection

When a user opens the Division dropdown:

- Display all available Bangladesh divisions.
- Allow the user to select one division.
- Retrieve only the districts belonging to that selected division.
- Reset any previously selected lower-level address values.

### Step 2 — District selection

When a user selects a district:

- Display only districts belonging to the selected division.
- Retrieve the relevant upazilas/thanas of that district.
- Reset previously selected upazila and union values.

### Step 3 — Upazila/Thana selection

When a user selects an upazila/thana:

- Display only upazilas/thanas belonging to the selected district.
- Retrieve only the unions or appropriate areas belonging to that selected upazila/thana.
- Reset any previously selected union/area value.

### Step 4 — Union/Area selection

When a user selects the final location:

- Save the correct geographic identifier.
- Save the correct parent relationships.
- Preserve the correct Bangla and English names when available.
- Make the selection available to checkout and order submission.

### Critical cascading rules

If the user changes Division:

- Clear District.
- Clear Upazila/Thana.
- Clear Union/Area.

If the user changes District:

- Clear Upazila/Thana.
- Clear Union/Area.

If the user changes Upazila/Thana:

- Clear Union/Area.

Never allow an invalid combination of unrelated geographic locations.

